<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <title><%= title %></title>
    <meta name="description"
        content="Echo — 1st Prize Winner out of 150+ teams at NSUT Oblivion Hackathon. An all-in-one music player and practice utility closing the gap between listening and learning. UI/UX Case Study by Drriti Pasrija.">

    <!-- Fonts: Outfit (Heading) + Plus Jakarta Sans (Body) -->
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Outfit:wght@400;500;600;700;800&family=Plus+Jakarta+Sans:wght@300;400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

    <!-- Icons -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.0/css/all.min.css">

    <!-- GSAP for scroll animations -->
    <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/gsap.min.js"></script>
    <script src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/gsap/3.12.2/ScrollTrigger.min.js"></script>

    <!-- Custom Case Study CSS -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/echo.css" />
</head>

<body>

    <!-- Reading Progress Indicator -->
    <div class="echo-progress-bar" id="echoProgressBar"></div>

    <!-- Floating Back Navigation -->
    <a href="/#work" class="echo-back-nav">
        <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i>
        <span>Back to Portfolio</span>
    </a>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
         1. HERO SECTION
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <header class="echo-hero">
        <div class="echo-badge-row">
            <span class="echo-badge echo-badge-winner">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-trophy"></i> 1st Prize Winner (150+ Teams)
            </span>
            <span class="echo-badge echo-badge-hackathon">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-bolt"></i> NSUT Oblivion Hackathon
            </span>
            <span class="echo-badge echo-badge-tag">
                <i class="fa-solid fa-music"></i> Product Design & UX Research
            </span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="echo-hero-title">Echo <span>Music</span></h1>
        <p class="echo-hero-tagline">Bridging the Gap Between Streaming Music and Learning It</p>

        <p class="echo-hero-description">
            Music streaming apps are built purely for passive listening, while music learning apps feel like rigid classrooms. 
            <strong>ECHO</strong> was designed to bridge this divide—transforming any streaming song into an interactive practice session 
            with live stem isolation, version-synced chords, tempo controls, and synced jam sessions.
        </p>

        <!-- Project Snapshot Meta Bar -->
        <div class="echo-meta-grid">
            <div class="echo-meta-item">
                <span>Role</span>
                <strong>UX Research & Product Design</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="echo-meta-item">
                <span>Team</span>
                <strong>2 Interns (Collaborative)</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="echo-meta-item">
                <span>Recognition</span>
                <strong>1st Prize · 150+ Teams</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="echo-meta-item">
                <span>Deliverables</span>
                <strong>User Flows, Competitive Matrix, Lo-Fi to Hi-Fi UI, Prototype</strong>
            </div>
            <div class="echo-meta-item">
                <span>Tools</span>
                <strong>Figma, FigJam, Protopie</strong>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Hero Showcase Banner -->
        <div class="echo-hero-showcase">
            <img src="/images/echo/round2-final-screens.jpg" 
                 alt="Echo Music Player and Practice Experience UI Screens" />
        </div>
    </header>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
         2. ROUND 1: THE INITIAL PROBLEM
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="echo-section">
        <div class="echo-container">
            <span class="echo-section-label">01 / Round 1 Exploration</span>
            <h2 class="echo-section-h2">The Problem With Modern Streaming Apps</h2>
            
            <p class="echo-body-text">
                During the opening round of the hackathon, we analyzed friction points across existing mainstream players like Spotify, Apple Music, and YouTube Music:
            </p>

            <div class="echo-split-grid">
                <div>
                    <ul style="list-style: none; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px;">
                        <li style="display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: flex-start;">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-ban" style="color: #ef4444; margin-top: 5px;"></i>
                            <div>
                                <strong style="color: #f1f5f9; display: block;">Cluttered Home Feeds</strong>
                                <span style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.95rem;">Algorithms push podcasts, audiobooks, and sponsored playlists, burying the user's personal saved library.</span>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li style="display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: flex-start;">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-ban" style="color: #ef4444; margin-top: 5px;"></i>
                            <div>
                                <strong style="color: #f1f5f9; display: block;">Friction in Active Queueing</strong>
                                <span style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.95rem;">Simple actions like adding a track to the queue require multiple clicks and interrupt the listening flow.</span>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li style="display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: flex-start;">
                            <i class="fa-solid fa-ban" style="color: #ef4444; margin-top: 5px;"></i>
                            <div>
                                <strong style="color: #f1f5f9; display: block;">Disconnected Social Listening</strong>
                                <span style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.95rem;">Sharing music and listening together is fragmented across separate messaging apps.</span>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div>
                    <div class="echo-callout-card" style="margin: 0;">
                        <p>
                            "We re-architected the primary user flow into three clear mental models: 
                            <strong>LISTEN</strong> (instant access to personal favorites), 
                            <strong>DISCOVER</strong> (contextual suggestions without feed overload), and 
                            <strong>CONNECT</strong> (live synced Jam sessions with friends)."
                        </p>
                        <small>— Round 1 UX Strategy</small>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Wireframes Showcase -->
            <div class="echo-showcase-card">
                <img src="/images/echo/round1-wireframes.jpg" 
                     alt="Low fidelity wireframes of Echo music player" 
                     class="echo-showcase-img" />
                <div class="echo-showcase-caption">
                    <span><strong>Round 1 Wireframes:</strong> Mapping home screen, queue drawer, and social jam room.</span>
                    <span class="echo-caption-tag">Information Architecture</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Screens Showcase -->
            <div class="echo-showcase-card">
                <img src="/images/echo/round1-final-screens.jpg" 
                     alt="High fidelity screens of Echo player and social music jam" 
                     class="echo-showcase-img" />
                <div class="echo-showcase-caption">
                    <span><strong>Round 1 Delivery:</strong> Home feed, full player, interactive Live Jam circle, and contextual search.</span>
                    <span class="echo-caption-tag">Visual Craft</span>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
         3. ROUND 2: THE CRITICAL PIVOT
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="echo-section">
        <div class="echo-container">
            <span class="echo-section-label">02 / Round 2 Pivot & Deep Discovery</span>
            <h2 class="echo-section-h2">The Musician's Dilemma: Listening vs. Learning</h2>
            
            <div class="echo-callout-card">
                <p style="font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 600; color: #ffffff;">
                    "Learning a song is rarely as simple as pressing play. Musicians constantly switch between 
                    music players, chord charts, tutorials, lyrics, and practice tools—making it nearly impossible 
                    to stay in sync with the exact version they're trying to learn."
                </p>
                <small>— Core Problem Statement</small>
            </div>

            <p class="echo-body-text">
                Under tight hackathon deadlines, we conducted rapid guerilla user interviews with guitarists, singers, 
                and hobbyist keyboard players. We synthesized their frustrations into an Empathy Map:
            </p>

            <!-- Empathy Map Summary Grid -->
            <div class="echo-split-grid" style="margin-top: 30px;">
                <div style="background: #14161f; padding: 28px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid var(--echo-card-border);">
                    <h4 style="color: var(--echo-purple-primary); font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 12px;">What Users Say & Think</h4>
                    <ul style="list-style: disc; margin-left: 20px; color: #cbd5e1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px;">
                        <li><em>"Wait, which YouTube video was I learning from again?"</em></li>
                        <li><em>"Is this chord sheet in the same key as the live album recording?"</em></li>
                        <li><em>"I lost my place again trying to rewind 5 seconds on my phone."</em></li>
                        <li><em>"This is taking forever... there must be an easier way."</em></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div style="background: #14161f; padding: 28px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid var(--echo-card-border);">
                    <h4 style="color: var(--echo-cyan); font-size: 1.1rem; margin-bottom: 12px;">What Users Do & Feel</h4>
                    <ul style="list-style: disc; margin-left: 20px; color: #cbd5e1; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px;">
                        <li>Switches between 3–4 open browser tabs (YouTube + Ultimate Guitar + Tuner + Metronome).</li>
                        <li>Constantly pauses, scrub-rewinds, and screenshots chord diagrams mid-video.</li>
                        <li>Feels overwhelmed, loses practice momentum, and gives up early.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Competitive Analysis Matrix -->
            <h3 style="font-family: var(--font-heading); font-size: 1.6rem; color: #ffffff; margin: 50px 0 20px;">
                Competitive Analysis Matrix
            </h3>

            <div class="echo-table-wrapper">
                <table class="echo-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Feature Dimension</th>
                            <th>Yousician</th>
                            <th>Ultimate Guitar</th>
                            <th>Moises.ai</th>
                            <th>ECHO (Our Strategy)</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Core Proposition</strong></td>
                            <td>Gamified practice lessons</td>
                            <td>Chord & tab community directory</td>
                            <td>AI audio stem isolation</td>
                            <td><strong>All-in-one streaming + practice utility</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Audio Catalog</strong></td>
                            <td>Synthesized MIDI / limited tracks</td>
                            <td>None (static text/tabs)</td>
                            <td>Requires manual MP3/WAV uploads</td>
                            <td><strong>Full streaming master catalog</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Live Stem Muting</strong></td>
                            <td>❌ (Pre-rendered tracks)</td>
                            <td>❌</td>
                            <td>✅ Market leader (AI stems)</td>
                            <td><strong>✅ Native 1-tap stem isolation</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Version Synced Chords</strong></td>
                            <td>⚠️ Gamified falling notes</td>
                            <td>⚠️ Tabs often mismatch live version</td>
                            <td>⚠️ Basic AI chord detection</td>
                            <td><strong>✅ Perfectly synced to exact track version</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><strong>Integrated Practice Tools</strong></td>
                            <td>Tempo control in lessons</td>
                            <td>Static autoscroll & metronome</td>
                            <td>A-B Looper & pitch shift</td>
                            <td><strong>✅ Native looper, count-in, transpose & stems</strong></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
         4. REJECTED FLOWS (CRITICAL THINKING)
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="echo-section">
        <div class="echo-container">
            <span class="echo-section-label">03 / Deliberate Decision Making</span>
            <h2 class="echo-section-h2">Why We Rejected Initial Flows</h2>

            <p class="echo-body-text">
                Top product teams judge designers by what they chose <em>not</em> to build. 
                Documenting our rejected flows helped us defend our decisions before the hackathon jury:
            </p>

            <div class="echo-showcase-card">
                <img src="/images/echo/rejected-flow.jpg" 
                     alt="Sketches and architectural diagram of rejected flows" 
                     class="echo-showcase-img" />
                <div class="echo-showcase-caption">
                    <span><strong>Artifact:</strong> Whiteboard sketches and decision tree documenting rejected concepts.</span>
                    <span class="echo-caption-tag">Design Rationale</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="echo-split-grid">
                <div style="background: #14161f; padding: 28px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #334155;">
                    <div style="display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 12px;">
                        <span style="background: #ef4444; color: #fff; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 999px;">REJECTED</span>
                        <strong style="color: #ffffff;">Rigid Role Toggle (Vocalist vs. Instrumentalist)</strong>
                    </div>
                    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">
                        <strong>Initial Idea:</strong> Make users choose either "Instrument Mode" or "Vocalist Mode" upfront.<br>
                        <strong>Issue Identified:</strong> Most real musicians sing while playing guitar or piano. Blending features was critical rather than siloing them.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div style="background: #14161f; padding: 28px; border-radius: 16px; border: 1px solid #334155;">
                    <div style="display: flex; gap: 10px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 12px;">
                        <span style="background: #ef4444; color: #fff; font-size: 0.75rem; font-weight: 700; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 999px;">REJECTED</span>
                        <strong style="color: #ffffff;">Manual Link Copy-Pasting</strong>
                    </div>
                    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.6;">
                        <strong>Initial Idea:</strong> Ask users to copy a YouTube/Spotify link and paste it into ECHO.<br>
                        <strong>Issue Identified:</strong> High cognitive friction.<br>
                        <strong>Solution:</strong> Implemented direct OS "Share to Echo" sheet to open the player in 1 tap.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
         5. FINAL PRODUCT & DEMO SCREENS
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section class="echo-section">
        <div class="echo-container">
            <span class="echo-section-label">04 / High Fidelity Product UI</span>
            <h2 class="echo-section-h2">From Casual Listening to Live Practice Session</h2>

            <p class="echo-body-text">
                The final interface introduces a clean 2-screen transition: tapping <strong>"Learn this song"</strong> on the full media player 
                expands the track into the synchronized Practice Suite.
            </p>

            <div class="echo-showcase-card">
                <img src="/images/echo/round2-final-screens.jpg" 
                     alt="Final UI screens showing Learning Suite, chord sync, and practice controls" 
                     class="echo-showcase-img" />
                <div class="echo-showcase-caption">
                    <span><strong>The Practice Suite:</strong> Synchronized lyrics, chords/tabs, role toggles (Guitar, Piano, Ukulele, Bass, Vocal), and tempo/looping controls.</span>
                    <span class="echo-caption-tag">Final Delivery</span>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Award Ceremony Spotlight -->
            <div class="echo-award-box">
                <img src="/images/echo/hackathon-first-prize.jpg" 
                     alt="Drriti Pasrija receiving 1st Prize certificate at Junoon NSUT Hackathon" 
                     class="echo-award-img" />
                <div class="echo-award-content">
                    <h3>🏆 Awarded 1st Prize Out of 150+ Teams</h3>
                    <p>
                        Presented at <em>Oppo Presents Oblivion</em> hosted by Junoon, NSUT. 
                        The jury praised our thorough persona research, the honest pivot from Round 1, 
                        and our deliberate decision to reject premature feature complexity in favor of real musician workflows.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════
         6. BOTTOM NAVIGATION
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <nav class="echo-bottom-nav">
        <a href="/khel-sutra" class="echo-bottom-link prev">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i>
            <span>Previous: Bhartiya Khel Sutra</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/mydayss" class="echo-bottom-link">
            <span>Next: MyDayss</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-right"></i>
        </a>
    </nav>

    <!-- Script for Progress Bar & Animations -->
    <script>
        window.addEventListener('scroll', () => {
            const winScroll = document.documentElement.scrollTop;
            const height = document.documentElement.scrollHeight - document.documentElement.clientHeight;
            const scrolled = (winScroll / height) * 100;
            document.getElementById('echoProgressBar').style.width = scrolled + '%';
        });

        gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger);

        gsap.utils.toArray('.echo-showcase-card, .echo-callout-card, .echo-award-box, .echo-table-wrapper').forEach(el => {
            gsap.from(el, {
                opacity: 0,
                y: 35,
                duration: 0.85,
                ease: "power2.out",
                scrollTrigger: {
                    trigger: el,
                    start: "top 85%",
                    toggleActions: "play none none none"
                }
            });
        });
    </script>
</body>

</html>
